# Copy to `.env` in this directory and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this example is tracked,
# which is why it holds no value.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Vite reads this file itself, from this directory. Only `VITE_`-prefixed names reach the app, and
# they are compiled into the bundle — so a value here is public by construction. Nothing secret
# belongs in this file; the API's own credentials live in `src/api/.env`, which no browser sees.
#
#   pnpm dev     # http://localhost:8443, which is what the API's AllowedOrigins defaults to

# -- Required. There is no default: `src/config.ts` refuses to start without one rather than
#    guessing, because a wrong guess is a request that silently goes nowhere.
#
#    This is the API's origin, not a path. `dotnet run` in `TrailBlaze.Api` serves it on 8080, and
#    so does the local stack in `src/api/docker-compose.yml`. Every route is prefixed with `/api`
#    or `/User` by the API itself, so none of that belongs here.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# -- Entra ID. Both or neither: with either one blank the app runs anonymously, the header shows a
#    disabled sign-in button, and every `[Authorize]` route is unreachable. That is a working
#    deployment, not a broken one — the public pages need no account — which is why a blank pair
#    is not an error here the way a blank `VITE_API_BASE_URL` is.
#
#    These two are identifiers rather than secrets, but they name a real tenant, so they stay
#    out of a tracked file. Copy them from the API deployment's `TenantId`/`Audience`: this is a
#    single-app registration, so the SPA client and the API audience are the same application.
VITE_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_ENTRA_TENANT_ID=

#    Optional. Blank derives `<VITE_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID>/.default`, which is the correct scope for this
#    registration: it declares no identifier URI, so the `api://<clientId>/.default` form names a
#    principal that does not exist and the sign-in fails with AADSTS500011.
VITE_ENTRA_SCOPE=
